# Everything committed here is published: GitHub Pages serves the whole repo at
# a guessable URL, so a file dropped in "just to look at" goes public the moment
# it is pushed. Working documents stay out of the repo entirely.
#
# The co-dev gallery images are exported copies in assets/img/art/ and are
# committed on purpose. It is the source documents that must not be.

# Full-resolution sources: team photos and art before they were resized into
# assets/. Around 145 MB, and every byte of it used to be committed. It was kept
# off the public site only by an accident of naming: with no .nojekyll file,
# GitHub Pages runs Jekyll, and Jekyll drops any directory starting with "_".
# Adding .nojekyll - a normal thing to do to speed up a static site - would have
# published the lot. Untracked now, so neither the site nor a clone carries it.
# Keep the originals somewhere backed up; they are not in this repo any more.
_originals/

# Decks, contracts, exports, anything sent over for reference
*.pdf
*.pptx
*.ppt
*.docx
*.doc
*.xlsx

# Project files that sometimes get dragged in alongside art exports
*.blend
*.blend1
*.psd
*.ztl

# OS clutter
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
